{
  "quest.00EB4D76000C0BD5.quest_desc": [
    "There are several types of &aFluids&r you can create. Some are just simple fuels used to create more power, while others are used to bind time and space.",
    "",
    "To create these fluids, you'll need to start by making &cPolymorphic Catalysts&r from Blazegold.",
    "",
    "Drop one of these into water to convert it to &6Polymorphic Fluid&r.",
  ],
  "quest.0B34E3B58783A93A.quest_desc": [
    "&cBlazegold Armor&r can be repaired by being thrown into &cLava&r, converting the lava into obsidian once repaired.",
  ],
  "quest.1C866721E1F2FF50.quest_desc": [
    "It's like a &aCoal Generator&r that fits into your pocket!",
    "",
    "It burns fuel sources to generate energy to power the items in your inventory!",
  ],
  "quest.7C7E949099FFC6DC.quest_desc": [
    "Probably the coolest upgrade you can make!",
    "",
    "The &dDrops Teleport Upgrade&r allows you to bind an inventory to a tool for drops to instantly teleport to when harvested.",
    "",
    "This is amazing for keeping your inventories clear when mining, or great on a Hoe for automatic harvesting!",
  ],
  "quest.105D29AEE67BE97B.quest_desc": [
    "Almost every tool in the mod has an &6Upgrade&r available for them.",
    "",
    "To use these, you'll need to create the Upgrade first, then combine it with the tool or armor piece inside of a &aSmithing Table&r.",
    "",
    "Note: Holding shift on the item will show you what upgrades are available for the tool! Some upgrades can only apply to higher tier items.",
  ],
  "quest.6AA6E514DB8A7E9E.quest_desc": [
    "Skip the cables with an &3Energy Transmitter&r. Connect it to a generator, set its area like any advanced machine, and it fills every block in that area that takes Forge Energy, at up to 1,000 FE per tick.",
    "",
    "The transfer loses 1% of the energy for every block it travels. Transmitters inside each other's areas balance their buffers with no loss, and the filter slots limit which machines get power.",
  ],
  "quest.34F33E80BC95E5A5.quest_desc": [
    "An &3Advanced Block Placer&r fills an area instead of a single spot. Its filter sets which blocks it may place on, and it respects the direction setting. With stone in the filter and the direction set to down, it only places on top of stone.",
  ],
  "quest.55EFDBD70D3464EB.quest_desc": [
    "Both fluid machines get an advanced version that covers an area instead of one block.",
    "",
    "Put a bucket of a fluid in the &3Advanced Fluid Collector&r's filter to collect only that fluid. The &3Advanced Fluid Placer&r's filter sets which blocks it may place fluid on, the same way the block placer's does.",
  ],
  "quest.7983727D0EE456FD.quest_desc": [
    "&eJust Dire Things&r has a very unique mechanic for acquiring its materials.",
    "",
    "It starts by making &bGoo&r which will spread onto other blocks to convert them over time.",
    "",
    "The first &bGoo&r that you'll make is called &aPrimogel Goo&r, which takes only a few basic materials.",
  ],
  "quest.389A8206E7B3A22C.title": "&aSimple Block Placer",
  "quest.103F400A68F9237F.title": "&3Inventory Holder and Player Accessor",
  "quest.58E70AA8656D1F55.title": "&3Experience Holder",
  "quest.4E0DB5D4574FD4E2.title": "&fUpgrade: Smelter",
  "quest.426758FCC5980BC9.quest_desc": [
    "Throw the &3Creature Catcher&r at a mob to catch it, and throw it again to let the mob out. Bosses and Ice and Fire creatures can't be caught.",
    "",
    "A filled catcher also works in the filter slots of advanced machines. With Compare NBT on, it matches the exact mob inside, down to a sheep's color.",
  ],
  "quest.5F3EDFC2E91BBE6E.quest_desc": [
    "&3Celestigem Tools&r uses &6Energy&r instead of durability and are a little better than Diamond-tier.",
    "",
    "With the &3Celestigem Hoe&r, you can use it to create &bVoidShimmer Soil&r.",
    "",
    "Upgrading your hoe with the &bDrops Teleport Upgrade&r and binding it to an inventory before tilling the soil will cause the crops to autoharvest directly into the bound inventory instead.",
    "",
    "At this tier, you can now combine the shovel, pickaxe, and axe to create the &3Celestigem Paxel&r.",
    "",
    "This tool can accept any of the upgrades for each of the tools used to craft it.",
  ],
  "quest.1C866721E1F2FF50.title": "&fPocket Generator",
  "task.4B459E2BBB4D1543.title": "&eJust Dire's &rFuel",
  "quest.27C9C8CEBC1464D1.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Stabilizer&r can be placed under your existing &aGoos&r to revive them using FE instead of feeding them items every now and then.",
  ],
  "quest.16180601C60DA378.title": "&fUpgrade: Night Vision",
  "quest.7F3C8670E66C77DF.quest_desc": [
    "The &3Portal Gun&r opens a pair of linked portals. Left-click fires the blue portal and Right-click fires the orange one, and players or items that go in one come out of the other.",
    "",
    "It runs on Forge Energy, holding 100,000 FE and using 1,000 FE per shot.",
  ],
  "quest.101457F50427E14E.title": "&cBlazejet Wand",
  "quest.426758FCC5980BC9.title": "&3Creature Catcher",
  "quest.16180601C60DA378.quest_desc": [
    "Automatic night vision, with none of the potion management.",
    "",
    "Craft the upgrade, then combine it with the armor piece in a Smithing Table. The effect runs as long as you wear the piece.",
  ],
  "quest.3404B0A29BF5A055.title": "&aSimple Fluid Collector",
  "quest.12512AAAF15B97C1.quest_desc": [
    "&2Time Fluid&r is used in the &dParadox Mixer&r and to power &dBudding Time Crystals&r.",
  ],
  "task.539B6E8AF9A4883C.title": "Ferricore Tools",
  "quest.35E0EDF360749CC9.title": "&fUpgrade: Elytra",
  "quest.34F33E80BC95E5A5.title": "&3Advanced Block Placer",
  "quest.5408C57600A556AE.title": "&aSimple Dropper",
  "quest.630661119379FA37.title": "&bJust Dyna Things",
  "quest.36E0D875AA8E2F66.quest_desc": [
    "This Goo can convert &6Netherite Blocks&r into &5Eclipse Alloy Ore&r.",
    "",
    "To activate it, you'll need to feed it either Sculk or Sculk Catalysts.",
    "",
    "Just like previous tiers, this can also convert all previous ingot blocks at an increased rate.",
  ],
  "quest.5B499DF961D9308B.quest_desc": [
    "A &2Simple Clicker&r block is a quite powerful little device. Despite being called simple, it has a few more options than the other simple machines.",
    "",
    "They're all straightforward though, try them on this note block here!",
  ],
  "quest.74394A0A56C5CFF5.title": "&fUpgrade: Mob Scanner",
  "quest.340D7F25B5EB0D33.quest_desc": [
    "The next tier of Goo is called &3VoidShimmer Goo&r, and allows you to convert Diamond Blocks into &bCelestigems&r.",
    "",
    "To activate it, you'll need to feed it either Ender Pearls or Chorus Fruit.",
    "",
    "Just like previous tiers, this Goo can also produce the previous resources, and at a faster rate.",
  ],
  "quest.001F0C36B4AB9F5F.title": "&a\"Simple\" &rFuel Generator",
  "quest.32D8D0691DF5B0F0.quest_desc": [
    "No fall damage, permanently.",
    "",
    "Pair it with the elytra upgrade and the worst outcome of a bad landing becomes an embarrassing one.",
  ],
  "quest.7F3C8670E66C77DF.title": "&3Portal Gun",
  "quest.32D8D0691DF5B0F0.title": "&fUpgrade: Negate Fall Damage",
  "quest.2E3D56F5BC1075DB.title": "&fUpgrade: Flight",
  "quest.630661119379FA37.quest_desc": [
    "&bJust Dyna Things&r is an addon mod for &eJust Dire Things&r which adds several new blocks and quality of life things to enhance your playthrough.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Note that the \", \"color\": \"gray\"}, {\"text\": \"Just Dyna Things guide\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,justdynathings:guide,justdynathings:index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Just Dyna Things guide\"}}, {\"text\": \" does not fully reflect the values configured for this pack.\", \"color\": \"gray\"}]",
  ],
  "quest.2A5BEEE03D74FCEE.title": "&dParadox Machine",
  "quest.3208C37E83A5C1FE.quest_desc": [
    "&dEclipse Alloy Tools&r are the highest tier from the mod.",
    "",
    "The &dEclipse Alloy Hoe&r can create the ultimate tier of farmland: &5Shadowpulse Soil&r. This farmland is the fastest and retains functionality.",
  ],
  "quest.335C4AD665DD967B.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\", \"The \", {\"text\": \"Advanced Portal Gun\", \"color\": \"light_purple\"}, \" remembers places. Press \", {\"keybind\": \"justdirethings.key.toggle_tool\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: V\"}}, \" to open its favorites menu, save the spot you're standing on, and fire a portal back to it later. It holds 1,000,000 FE and uses 5,000 FE per shot.\"]",
    "",
    "Each shot also uses &dPortal Fluid&r. To make it, drop a &3Portal Fluid Catalyst&r into &bPolymorphic Fluid&r while in the End. That gives &bUnstable Portal Fluid&r, which breaks down outside the End. An active &3VoidShimmer Goo&r or higher next to the source turns it into stable Portal Fluid in about 2 minutes.",
    "",
    "Fill the gun by Right-clicking a Portal Fluid source, or with a &3Fluid Canister&r.",
  ],
  "quest.4BF73E8B9214BF65.quest_desc": [
    "Built from a &bBlazejet Wand&r, the &3Voidshift Wand&r keeps Air Burst and adds Void Shift, which teleports you to the block you're looking at, up to a set distance.",
    "",
    "Open the tool settings screen to choose the key or mouse button for each ability and to shorten the maximum distance.",
  ],
  "quest.20AC15DC1E6E47D7.title": "&fUpgrade: Smoker",
  "quest.15D80251D92D6A3C.quest_desc": [
    "&5Shadowpulse Goo&r can also be used to convert &9Budding Amethyst&r into &6Budding Time Crystal Blocks&r. ",
    "",
    "To create and harvest &6Time Crystals&r from these, you'll need to make use of &cSwapper&r machines.",
    "",
    "To start, place the Budding Time Crystal block in the overworld (also works for other overworld-like dimensions).",
    "",
    "After a little bit of time, the block will make a noise and change colors. It means it's ready to be moved!",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "The next step will be moving the Budding Time Crystal block to the &cNether&r for it to absorb more energy there. Just like before, it will make a sound and change colors when ready.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Finally, you'll need to transport the Budding block to the &dEnd&r.",
    "",
    "It will absorb the dimension's energies and start to grow &6Time Crystals&r. Be careful not to harvest any crystal that isn't fully grown!",
    "",
    "Over time, it will lose the energies it has absorbed and will need to be brought back to each dimension to recharge. This means you'll need to move the small crystal buds as well!",
    "",
    "To move the block and growing crystals, you'll need to use the &cAdvanced Swapper&r.",
  ],
  "quest.7613CBF890767732.title": "&3Advanced Clicker",
  "quest.73CA8F7C9D10133F.quest_desc": [
    "The &aHammer&r upgrade increases the area of effect for the tool it is installed into based on the tier of the tool.",
    "",
    "For example, installing this in a &cBlazegold Pickaxe&r will allow you to mine in a 3x3 area.",
  ],
  "quest.5B499DF961D9308B.title": "&aSimple Clicker",
  "quest.2C55C6EBABA86BA8.quest_desc": [
    "This &aSimple Block Breaker&r is bound and determined to use its tool to break the block in front of it. Even if the tool is a stick and the block is obsidian. It'll get there.",
  ],
  "quest.678D5A29CA06C587.quest_desc": [
    "When installed in an &dEclipse Alloy Sword&r, this upgrade can be used to see mobs through walls.",
  ],
  "quest.3F26B10626145BBC.title": "&aJust Dire's Item Collector",
  "quest.66CE1E98DC5045DC.quest_desc": [
    "A &aSimple Sensor&r gives off a redstone signal when it sees a matching block or mob in front of it. Its target button cycles through blocks, air, hostile, passive, adult, child, player, all living and dropped items.",
    "",
    "With a block in the filter slot, Right-click the slot to match a block state instead, such as a door being open or a lever being on.",
    "",
    "The &3Advanced Sensor&r counts matches across an area. Set it to fewer than 10 adult cows and it can switch on a clicker to feed them.",
  ],
  "quest.3208C37E83A5C1FE.title": "&dEclipse Alloy Tools",
  "quest.103F400A68F9237F.quest_desc": [
    "An &3Inventory Holder&r is a storage block laid out like your own inventory, with armor and offhand slots. Ctrl-click an item inside to lock that slot to it. The swap button trades your whole inventory with the block's, which makes switching between a mining kit and a combat kit quick.",
    "",
    "The &3Player Accessor&r lets pipes and hoppers reach your inventory. Each face can point at a different part of it, such as armor on the top and your offhand on the bottom.",
  ],
  "quest.55EFDBD70D3464EB.title": "&3Advanced Fluid Machines",
  "quest.417573A657CAED05.quest_desc": [
    "Once you've gathered some materials from the &cNether&r, you can upgrade to the next tier of Goo.",
    "",
    "&cBlazebloom Goo&r will allow you to create a new tier of metal called &6Blazegold&r by converting Blocks of Gold, just like we did with Iron.",
    "",
    "To activate it, you'll need to feed it either Nether Wart or Blaze Powder.",
    "",
    "It also retains the ability to create &aFerricore Ore&r, so no need to make another Primogel Goo just for Iron. It converts Iron faster than Primogel too!",
  ],
  "quest.39A6CE8A1D5B2D8F.quest_desc": [
    "Don't be fooled; the &aSimple Coal Generator&r from &eJust Dire Things&r takes burning coal to a new level.",
    "",
    "While this can burn regular burnable items like coal or wood, it can also burn the different tiers of coal from the mod itself, like &aPrimal Coal&r!",
    "",
    "The higher the coal tier, the more power per piece.",
  ],
  "quest.3F26B10626145BBC.quest_desc": [
    "The &aItem Collector&r from &eJust Dire Things&r is a highly configurable collector.",
    "",
    "Inside of the interface, you can adjust the radius up to a max of 11x11x11, but can also offset where the machine collects if needed.",
    "",
    "You can also adjust even more options like filtering which items it can pick up, or how fast it picks items up.",
  ],
  "task.56C7704FDEA55380.title": "&cBlazegold Tools",
  "task.1A14716B7F473DC5.title": "Just Dyna Things",
  "quest.7C11CB5E04CA381F.quest_desc": [
    "&cBlazegold Tools&r can be repaired by being thrown into &cLava&r, converting the lava into obsidian once repaired.",
    "",
    "When using a &cBlazegold Hoe&r to till dirt, you'll create &cBlazebloom Soil&r. This soil grows crops faster and autoharvests fully grown crops by itself.",
    "",
    "When this happens, the items will only stay in the world for about 2 seconds! Make sure to collect them using an &aItem Collector&r.",
  ],
  "quest.340D7F25B5EB0D33.title": "&fMaking &3Celestigems",
  "quest.4BF73E8B9214BF65.title": "&3Voidshift Wand",
  "quest.389A8206E7B3A22C.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSimple Block Placer&r places blocks. Simple!",
    "",
    "You'll want this for many automations. Get creative!",
  ],
  "quest.012AEBFDB1F1512E.title": "Ferricore Armor",
  "quest.2F057F981B68EB95.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSimple Fluid Placer&r takes a fluid input and puts it in the world for all to see.",
  ],
  "quest.001F0C36B4AB9F5F.quest_desc": [
    "If you think the Simple Coal Generator is good, you should try out the &aSimple Fuel Generator&r.",
    "",
    "Instead of burning coal, this uses the special &6Fuels&r from the mod, and the top tier fuel is worth 4,000 FE per mB.",
  ],
  "quest.0E107AC18FCFDB57.quest_desc": [
    "Now that we have some &aPrimogel Goo&r, we can use it to see how this mechanic works.",
    "",
    "Start by placing down the &aPrimogel Goo&r somewhere in an open space, then activate it by giving it either Sugar or Rotten Flesh. You can now place &2Iron Blocks&r on any of its faces to start the conversion.",
    "",
    "{image\\:\\ftb:textures/quests/direthings/impure_daisy.png width:200 height:100 align:center}",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "You'll notice the Goo slowly starting to spread over, taking it completely over. Once the process is complete, you'll be left with &aRaw Ferricore Ore&r.",
    "",
    "&7&oSome Shaders will not properly display this effect, so you might want to disable them if you want to see the changes.",
    "",
    "Mining this ore will give you &aRaw Ferricore&r, which you can smelt down into &2Ferricore Ingots&r.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Fortune does not work on these ores. You will typically get between 3 or 4 raw ores.",
  ],
  "quest.565AF0E2D4AB41BE.quest_desc": [
    "&eJust Dire Things&r grows its own ores. You feed a &bGoo&r block, it eats the block next to it, and what comes out is the mod's metal. From there it's gadgets, tools and armor, most of them a bit overpowered.",
    "",
    "To get started with this mod, you'll need to craft the &aPrimogel Goo&r.",
  ],
  "quest.335C4AD665DD967B.title": "&dAdvanced Portal Gun",
  "quest.64B237B611F88036.quest_desc": [
    "&dEclipse Alloy Armor&r is the highest tier from the mod.",
  ],
  "quest.292BF6C7378B6C46.quest_desc": [
    "Unlike the other advanced machines, the &3Advanced Dropper&r can't grow its area, but its offset lets it drop items several blocks away. It holds a 3x3 grid of items.",
    "",
    "The filter slots set which items drop and in what order. Cobblestone then redstone drops one of each in turn, and it waits whenever either runs out.",
  ],
  "quest.66E2432429FD3ED9.title": "&3Advanced Block Breaker",
  "quest.183F42AD35A76E98.title": "&dTime Wand",
  "quest.101457F50427E14E.quest_desc": [
    "The &cBlazejet Wand&r is a great tool for getting around.",
    "",
    "This wand comes with the &aAir Burst&r ability. When used, it will boost you forward a few blocks.",
    "",
    "You can even upgrade it to unlock even more abilities!",
  ],
  "quest.2E3D56F5BC1075DB.quest_desc": [
    "When installed in the &dEclipse Alloy Chestplate&r, this upgrade allows you to have creative flight.",
  ],
  "quest.2B6A88AA896C54A6.title": "&fUpgrade: Ore X-Ray",
  "quest.6AA6E514DB8A7E9E.title": "&3Energy Transmitter",
  "quest.7613CBF890767732.quest_desc": [
    "Mob farms and animal breeders both run on the &3Advanced Clicker&r. It clicks across an area and can filter blocks or mobs. To filter a mob, put a spawn egg or a filled &3Creature Catcher&r in its filter slots.",
    "",
    "Set it to left-click hostiles to fight, or to right-click adult animals while it holds their food to breed them.",
  ],
  "quest.565AF0E2D4AB41BE.title": "&fWelcome to &eJust Dire Things&r!",
  "quest.2B6A88AA896C54A6.quest_desc": [
    "When used, this upgrade will allow x-ray vision of all ores through the walls around you.",
  ],
  "quest.46C2C45AE017AE81.quest_desc": [
    "When equipped to a &aJust Dire's Pickaxe&r, right-clicking will activate the ability and make nearby ores glow through walls.",
  ],
  "quest.105D29AEE67BE97B.title": "&fTool &aUpgrades",
  "quest.35E0EDF360749CC9.quest_desc": [
    "A built-in elytra, so the chestplate slot stops being a choice between armor and flight.",
    "",
    "You still need fireworks or a launch to get moving. What you no longer need is somewhere safe to stash your chestplate.",
  ],
  "quest.58E70AA8656D1F55.quest_desc": [
    "Your levels are safe in an &3Experience Holder&r. The + and - buttons move 1 level between you and the block, Shift moves 10 and Ctrl moves all of them.",
    "",
    "Give it a target level and a redstone mode, and it keeps players in its area at that level. At 30 beside an enchanting table, it tops you back up after every enchant. It can also collect experience orbs from its area.",
    "",
    "It works as a tank of liquid experience too, at 20 mB per point, and keeps its contents when broken.",
  ],
  "quest.4F3787D3DCAFBB6F.title": "&fUpgrade: Instant Break",
  "quest.3404B0A29BF5A055.quest_desc": [
    "The &2Simple Fluid Collector&r collects in world fluids, without needing a bucket or such. Great for infinite water sources!",
  ],
  "quest.012AEBFDB1F1512E.quest_desc": [
    "&aFerricore&r is the first full set the mod gives you, and it is worth wearing long before it is worth admiring.",
    "",
    "The set itself is ordinary. What matters is that every piece takes upgrades, so this is the armor you start bolting abilities onto.",
  ],
  "quest.292BF6C7378B6C46.title": "&3Advanced Dropper",
  "quest.4E0DB5D4574FD4E2.quest_desc": [
    "Installing the &cSmelter&r upgrade activates &cAutosmelting&r.",
  ],
  "quest.1A89ACDC528588D5.quest_desc": [
    "&3Celestigem Armor&r uses &6Energy&r instead of durability and are a little better than Diamond-tier.",
  ],
  "quest.20AC15DC1E6E47D7.quest_desc": [
    "This upgrade works just like the Smelter upgrade, and allows you to autosmelt mob drops when installed.",
  ],
  "quest.678D5A29CA06C587.title": "&fUpgrade: Mob X-Ray",
  "quest.5408C57600A556AE.quest_desc": [
    "Tired of vanilla droppers needing redstone and throwing items everywhere? Try the &aSimple Dropper&r! You can precisely control quantity and throughput with these.",
  ],
  "quest.7C7E949099FFC6DC.title": "&fUpgrade: Drops Teleport",
  "quest.5DF40808F9C6FEC0.title": "&fUseful Machine Tools",
  "quest.15D80251D92D6A3C.title": "&fAltering &dTime",
  "quest.27C9C8CEBC1464D1.title": "&6Stabilizer",
  "quest.66E2432429FD3ED9.quest_desc": [
    "Where the simple version breaks one block, the &3Advanced Block Breaker&r breaks a whole area. Turn on Render Area in its screen, then use the RAD buttons to grow the area and the OFF buttons to move it.",
    "",
    "Its filter has two modes. Filter Block matches the blocks themselves, and Filter Item matches their drops, so cobblestone in Filter Item mode breaks both stone and cobblestone.",
  ],
  "quest.5DF40808F9C6FEC0.quest_desc": [
    "Once you have &aFerricore&r, you can make most of the simple machines the mod offers.",
    "",
    "With new machines, it wouldn't hurt to make the &aFerricore Wrench&r. This tool can rotate machines by right-clicking, or Sneak + Right-clicking will insta-break them for you.",
    "",
    "The &aMachine Settings Copier&r does exactly what you think! Sneak + Right-clicking on a machine with it will copy the settings to the copier, then right-clicking on a different machine will paste the settings.",
  ],
  "quest.73CA8F7C9D10133F.title": "&fUpgrade: Hammer",
  "quest.46C2C45AE017AE81.title": "&fUpgrade: Ore Scanner",
  "quest.74394A0A56C5CFF5.quest_desc": [
    "When equipped in a &aJust Dire's Sword&r, this upgrade allows you to scan for nearby mobs by right-clicking with the sword.",
  ],
  "task.7596A251AEDB6E3B.title": "&3Celestigem Tools",
  "task.78AD19380F54B22A.title": "&6Just Dire's &rEmpowered Coal",
  "quest.36E0D875AA8E2F66.title": "&5Ore of the Eclipse",
  "quest.1A89ACDC528588D5.title": "&3Celestigem Armor",
  "quest.64B237B611F88036.title": "&dEclipse Alloy Armor",
  "quest.7983727D0EE456FD.title": "&fIt All Starts With &aGoo",
  "quest.417573A657CAED05.title": "&fCreating &cBlazegold",
  "quest.2F057F981B68EB95.title": "&aSimple Fluid Placer",
  "quest.2C55C6EBABA86BA8.title": "&aSimple Block Breaker",
  "quest.0B34E3B58783A93A.title": "&cBlazegold Armor",
  "quest.4F3787D3DCAFBB6F.quest_desc": [
    "Who needs efficiency enchants when you can just break things instantly?",
  ],
  "quest.2A5BEEE03D74FCEE.quest_desc": [
    "Mined-out ore can come back with the &dParadox Machine&r. Set its area, make sure the ore blocks or mobs you want are inside, and press the snapshot button. After you mine the ores or kill the mobs, running the machine restores them.",
    "",
    "Each run costs a lot of power and &dTime Fluid&r, and the mobs that return may differ a little from the originals.",
    "",
    "&cHeavy use builds up paradox energy, shown in its screen. Too much opens a Paradox that grows and swallows blocks, items and mobs for good. Throw a &dTime Crystal&r into it to seal it.",
  ],
  "task.2511CEBC75D203CA.title": "Any &aEclipse Alloy&r Tool",
  "quest.183F42AD35A76E98.quest_desc": [
    "Anything that ticks, from furnaces to crops, runs faster under the &dTime Wand&r. Each Right-click doubles the speed, up to 256 times normal, and the boost lasts 30 seconds.",
    "",
    "It runs on Forge Energy and &dTime Fluid&r, and faster speeds use more of both.",
  ],
  "quest.39A6CE8A1D5B2D8F.title": "&a\"Simple\" &rCoal Generator",
  "quest.0E107AC18FCFDB57.title": "&aGoo Transmutations",
  "quest.66CE1E98DC5045DC.title": "&3Sensors",
  "quest.1C69F681EC14CCF1.quest_desc": [
    "&aFerricore tools&r are a little better than Iron and most can be equipped with &bUpgrades&r.",
    "",
    "The &aFerricore Hoe&r to till dirt will create &2Primogel Soil&r, which works a little faster than standard farmland.",
  ],
}